---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Wobbly from "../components/Wobbly.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
import { icons } from "../data/icons";
import { hash, sampleIcon } from "../../../packages/icons/lib/geometry.mjs";
import { toPathData } from "../../../packages/icons/lib/svg.mjs";
import canvas from "../../../packages/icons/defs/canvas.mjs";

const seeds = ["square", "square-2", "square-3"].map((seed) => ({
  seed,
  d: sampleIcon(canvas.square, hash(seed)).map(toPathData).join(""),
}));
---

<Base title="The story · zicons" description="Where the zicons came from, and the few rules every icon is drawn by.">
  <article class="prose-sk pt-10">
    <span class="tape">the story</span>
    <Wobbly text="from zketch, with love" tag="h1" class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2.6rem,7vw,4.6rem)]" />

    <div class="placeholder card mt-10">
      <span class="tape pin">zero: write the zketch story here</span>
      <p class="hand text-2xl">A few lines in your own words, for example:</p>
      <ul class="hand text-xl">
        <li>why Zketch needed its own icons instead of an off-the-shelf set</li>
        <li>how you made them, and what you wanted them to feel like</li>
        <li>what you hope people make with them</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10">
      zicons is the icon set from <a href={SITE.zketch}>Zketch</a>, the drawing app. There are {icons.length} of them so far.
    </p>

    <h2>How they're drawn</h2>
    <p>
      Every icon is written as a centreline, a single pen path, and then traced with the same brush. A few rules keep the
      whole set feeling like one pen drew it.
    </p>

    <div class="rules mt-8">
      <figure class="board card">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="board-svg zi-boil" aria-hidden="true">
          <g class="board-grid">
            {Array.from({ length: 25 }, (_, k) => <line x1={k} y1="0" x2={k} y2="24" />)}
            {Array.from({ length: 25 }, (_, k) => <line x1="0" y1={k} x2="24" y2={k} />)}
          </g>
          <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" class="board-live" />
          <path d={icons.find((i) => i.name === "pencil")!.d} class="board-icon" />
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="hand">the 24 px grid, with the 3..21 live area dashed</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="rule-list">
        <li><strong>A 24 by 24 grid.</strong> The drawing stays roughly inside 3..21, so icons line up at any size.</li>
        <li><strong>One even line, 2.2 wide.</strong> Round caps, round joins, no fills. Colour comes from the text around it.</li>
        <li><strong>Rounded corners everywhere.</strong> Nothing ends in a sharp point; a pen doesn't either.</li>
        <li><strong>Few strokes.</strong> Each stroke is one pen movement, and most icons need two or three.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>The bow</h2>
    <p>
      Straight edges bow very slightly, the way a ruler-free line does. The bow is seeded from the icon's name, so every
      build draws exactly the same line, but no two icons wobble alike. Here is the same square drawn with three seeds:
    </p>
    <div class="seeds mt-6">
      {seeds.map((s) => (
        <figure class="card">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="96" height="96" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d={s.d} />
          </svg>
          <figcaption class="hand">seed “{s.seed}”</figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>The boil</h2>
    <p>
      On this site the lines never sit perfectly still. That shimmer is called line boil: in traditional animation every
      frame is traced again, so the lines jitter a little. Here it's a small SVG filter that nudges each line about eight times
      a second. The icons themselves don't move; the boil is something you add on top, and you can add it to your own
      pages with the <a href="/use#wobble">wobble helper</a>. If it bothers you, the boil switch at the top turns it off.
    </p>

    <div class="cta card mt-12">
      <Icon name="brush" size={40} plain boil="big" />
      <div>
        <p class="hand m-0 text-3xl">Want to draw with them?</p>
        <p class="m-0">They live in Zketch's toolbar. Open it and doodle something.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn sk btn-accent ml-auto" href={SITE.zketch}>Open Zketch</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .placeholder {
    position: relative;
    padding: 30px 26px 18px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 0 12px, #ffd9661f 12px 24px), var(--card);
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .pin {
    position: absolute;
    top: -16px;
    left: 22px;
  }
  .placeholder ul {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .rules {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 320px) 1fr;
    gap: 34px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .board {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .board-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .board-grid line {
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 12%, transparent);
    stroke-width: 0.04;
  }
  .board-live {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 0.1;
    stroke-dasharray: 0.4 0.3;
  }
  .board-icon {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2.2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .board figcaption {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .rule-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .rule-list li {
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .seeds {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .seeds figure {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 20px 10px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .seeds figure:nth-child(2) {
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }
  .seeds figure:nth-child(3) {
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }
  .seeds figcaption {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 18px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .rules {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
